  "title": "# Full AmberX app API exposed as MCP tools via axHub Brett wants Claude to be able to do everything…",
  "asked": "# Full AmberX app API exposed as MCP tools via axHub Brett wants Claude to be able to do everything in the AmberX app through axHub: notes, to-dos (create, edit, check off, change status, delete), and every other app feature/section that holds user data or actions. 1. Audit the AmberX app (Android + backend) and list every feature with data or actions. 2. Build an API covering all of it (CRUD + status changes), reusing the existing AXPP/axHub device channel the recorder uses. 3. Expose each as tools on the axHub `amberx` service so Claude can call them. Reads = allow. Deletes and anything destructive = confirm. Recorder start keeps its existing Approve. 4. If axHub needs changes, write them up clearly in the PR (separate axHub PR only if required). 5. Tests for each tool group. Update install/setup docs. 6. Open PR(s); do not merge or deploy. Rules: no sub-agents, never print secrets, clean commits, short phone-readable PR description. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, patches-web, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once.",
